Apparently T_OBS is the reference observation time for AIA and HMI metadata, at least for Level-1 data products.  (DATE-OBS is derived from T_OBS by subtracting half the exposure time, so would not be a reference time.)  That means that we should use T_OBS for constructing the coordinate frame and observer location.  With #7682, we can now simply override the `reference_date` property so that T_OBS is used.

